================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================

- "Grok Bot says I don't have access": SuperGrok Lite isn't supported. Upgrade or use a paid Cursor plan, then link it in Settings -> Usage & Billing.

- "I can't add a seventh Bot": A group holds six Bots max. Remove one before adding another.

- "A Bot asked for my broker password or wallet": Deny it. Bots should only use the official connectors from Part 10, never your login. Remind it: "Read desk/my-rules.md."

- "Robinhood sign-in failed": Finish the login and tap Allow within a few minutes, since the link expires after about 15. If it still fails on your phone, connect once from the desktop app, and the connector carries over to your phone.

- "It wrote the order but didn't place it": Some modes draft an order and stop. Reply "place the order now, exactly as on card #id".

- "Two Bots gave different prices": That's Skeptic doing its job. Ask for fresh sources (see "Double-check a card") and check the number yourself. Sites sometimes block bots or show old data.

- "My routine didn't post anything": If nothing met your rules, it stays quiet on purpose. Otherwise open the Bot -> View conversation details -> Routines, check the history and choose Test run.

- "I don't see the approval in the group": Approval cards only show up in a Bot's one-to-one chat. Open that Bot from the sidebar.

- "The group is too noisy": Tell Chief: "Only post in the group when something changes, and @mention one owner per step."

- "I'm burning through my usage": Cut Scout's routine to once a day, ask for shorter reports, and pause the evening report on weekends. Big browsing jobs use the most.


